### Session 2 practice solution: the Publisher routes.
### Use the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy these into Postman.

### All publishers (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/publishers

### One publisher (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/publishers/1

### An id that matches nothing (404)
GET http://localhost:3000/publishers/999

### An id that is not a number (400)
GET http://localhost:3000/publishers/abc

### Add a publisher (201). The client supplies the id, because no primary key is IDENTITY.
POST http://localhost:3000/publishers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": 900, "name": "Mulberry Books" }

### Change a publisher name (200, or 404 if the id does not exist)
PUT http://localhost:3000/publishers/900
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Mulberry Books Ltd" }

### Remove a publisher (204, no body, or 404 if the id does not exist)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/publishers/900
